                <pb facs="0833" n="734" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg734"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.115/112: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Barcelona</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Perkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Barcelona</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-10-09T12:00:00+00:00">October 9,
                        1936—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 4:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My telegram of October 8, 8 p.m. Councilor of Economy expressed surprise last
                    night at news of proposed cotton seizure and asked for <pb facs="0834" n="735"
                        xml:id="pg735"/> original communication of labor organization to
                    International Banking Corporation in order to lay matter before a meeting of
                    Council today. He promised to notify Consulate General and International Banking
                    Corporation of result of meeting. Embassy at Madrid informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
